What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/apple-h2fmi/<device>/flash_trace_sequence
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-mtd@lists.infradead.org
Description:
		Read-only boundary for the apple_h2fmi_transaction trace event.
		The two decimal numbers are the probe generation and the latest
		event sequence allocated by that driver instance. Generation one
		identifies the first probe of the built-in driver. A second probe
		cannot establish coverage from the start of the boot.

		Sequence numbers start at one. They advance for request entry,
		writes to the NAND command register, status polls, and request
		returns. A gap in a capture indicates a lost or filtered event.
		A snapshot can cut through an active request. Read the boundary
		with the workload quiescent to check complete requests.

		The attribute returns ENODATA if the tracepoint was disabled when
		the driver probed. Reading the attribute does not access flash.
